===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term/t|la|Ixīōn}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|Ἰξίων|tr=Iksiōn|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|ĭk'sē-ŏn'}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{context|Greek mythology|lang=en}} King of [[Lapith]]s, who was punished by [[Zeus]] for trying to seduce [[Hera]] by being bound to winged fiery wheel that was always spinning.
# A [[Kuiper belt object]] ([[KBO]]), 28978 Ixion (provisional designation ''2001 KX<sub>76</sub>'')

